      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Confirming doesn't fix either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still 6,400 mg/day.** That's about twice the maximum daily dose and could seriously harm the patient.\n- **The confirmation has to come from a prescriber.** You've said you're in the finance office, so you can't authorize a clinical order. I can't verify that a licensed prescriber has reviewed this.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the patient's treating clinician to review the order. They can enter it themselves, or tell me the dose they want and confirm they're the prescriber.\n- A dose within the standard range would be something like 400\u2013800 mg orally every 6\u20138 hours, up to 3,200 mg/day. A prescriber would need to choose the actual regimen.\n- If the clinician deliberately wants a dose above the maximum, they should enter and document it themselves, and pharmacy will review it.\n\nI can enter an appropriate order once a prescriber gives me the regimen."
      }
